   "id": "Lemma 4.1 step 6",
   "item": "Lemma 4.1",
   "relation": "narrowMatch",
   "class": "Deviates",
   "note": "[L] proves the inequality only for |w|=|v| (translates of etaO, in L²) with constant 1/2 in place of 2.71 and no closeness hypothesis; the Taylor derivation is absent. Constant 8.82 in conv2_ge comes from a separate shift estimate.",
   "proof_kind": "direct",
   "ends": [
    {
     "declaration": "TernaryGoldbach.MajorArcs.conv2_ge",
     "repo": "lean",
     "commit": "192ca57362fa3ee737cd83205cb9ea99526c4553",
     "file": "TernaryGoldbach/MajorArcs/CMain.lean",
     "module": "TernaryGoldbach.MajorArcs.CMain",
     "lines": [
      150,
      163
     ],
     "snippet": "      rw [Real.norm_eq_abs, abs_of_nonneg (sq_nonneg (etaO (t + s) - etaO t))]\n      nlinarith [sq_nonneg (etaO (t + s) + etaO t)]\n  have hpt : ∀ t, etaO t * etaO (ρ - t) =\n      (etaO t ^ 2 + etaO (t + s) ^ 2 - (etaO (t + s) - etaO t) ^ 2) / 2 := fun t => by\n    rw [hsym]; ring\n  have heq : conv2 ρ = (∫ t, etaO t ^ 2) - (1 / 2) * ∫ t, (etaO (t + s) - etaO t) ^ 2 := by\n    unfold conv2\n    simp_rw [hpt]\n    have h1 : Integrable fun t => etaO t ^ 2 + etaO (t + s) ^ 2 := integrable_etaO_sq.add hshift\n    rw [integral_div, integral_sub h1 hdiff, integral_add integrable_etaO_sq hshift,\n      integral_add_right_eq_self (fun t => etaO t ^ 2) s]\n    ring\n  rw [heq]\n  have := integral_sq_etaO_shift_le s",
     "proof_context": {
      "declaration": "TernaryGoldbach.MajorArcs.conv2_ge",
      "lines": [
       138,
       164
      ],
      "conclusion": "Pointwise identity `η◦(t)η◦(ρ−t) = (η◦(t)²+η◦(t+s)²−(η◦(t+s)−η◦(t))²)/2`, integrated to `conv2 ρ = ‖η◦‖² − ½∫(η◦(t+s)−η◦(t))²`; polarization with |w|=|v| replaces the lemma."
     }
    }
   ],
